{
  "_comment": "Mira's model registry — labels, pricing, and per-purpose recommendations for the dashboard and cost estimates. Selection is not limited to this list: the dashboard merges the backend's live catalog and accepts free-form ids. Format mirrors a trimmed subset of LiteLLM's model_prices_and_context_window.json so users familiar with that file recognize the shape.",
  "_fields": {
    "label": "Display name shown in the dashboard dropdown.",
    "provider": "Underlying provider (anthropic, openai, google, etc.) — purely informational.",
    "max_input_tokens": "Hard cap on input tokens. Used to size prompt-trimming logic.",
    "max_output_tokens": "Hard cap on output tokens per response. Used as the default max_tokens for completions.",
    "input_cost_per_1m": "USD per 1M input tokens.",
    "output_cost_per_1m": "USD per 1M output tokens.",
    "supports_json_mode": "Whether the model honors response_format=json_object.",
    "purposes": "Roles this model is allowed for: 'indexing', 'review', or both.",
    "recommended_for": "Roles where this model is the recommended default (shown with a Recommended badge).",
    "endpoint": "Optional. The provider profile (providers.json) this id is served by, for endpoints whose ids are not OpenRouter-style. Such an entry is offered only when that profile is the configured endpoint, never on OpenRouter or Bedrock.",
    "api_style": "Optional, with endpoint. The protocol this model is served over on that endpoint when it is not the endpoint's own: 'responses' or 'chat'. Calls to it go out that way whatever the endpoint is set to (models.dev says the same for the models it knows).",
    "monthly_limit_usd": "Informational. On a subscription endpoint, the model's monthly allowance in USD as the provider documents it.",
    "cache_read_cost_per_1m": "Optional. USD per 1M input tokens served from the provider's prompt cache. Cached tokens are billed at this rate in cost estimates; absent, they cost the input rate.",
    "cache_write_cost_per_1m": "Informational. USD per 1M tokens written to the prompt cache, where the provider bills that separately. Not used in estimates: most endpoints do not report cache writes.",
    "credit_multiplier": "Optional. On a subscription billed in plan credits, credits consumed per USD of usage value (OpenDesign's Coding Plan multiplier: 0.27 for DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Eco, 0.5 for Flash). Defaults to 1.",
    "off_peak": "Optional. {\"hours_utc\": \"16:30-00:30\", ...price fields} — the rates (and credit_multiplier) that apply inside that UTC window, for a model priced lower off-peak. Without hours_utc, DeepSeek's published window (16:30-00:30 UTC) is used.",
    "long_context": "Optional. {\"above_tokens\": N, ...price fields} — the rates that apply once a call's prompt exceeds N tokens, for a model with a long-context tier.",
    "_scoped_keys": "An entry keyed '<id>@<endpoint>' (e.g. 'deepseek-v4.1-flash@open-design') belongs to that provider profile alone, so the same id can be priced differently on two endpoints. Looked up for that endpoint it wins over the plain '<id>' entry; everywhere else it reads as if it had \"endpoint\": \"<endpoint>\". No need to repeat the endpoint field inside it."
  },

